{
  "about": "CSV through Clarity.Formats (docs/FORMATS-PLAN.md, step 2): `read list<Item> from csv text` and `csv of items`. RFC 4180: fields separated by a comma (option `separator`, `\\\\t` for a tab), quoted with `\"` (option `quote`) where they hold a separator, a quote or a line break, a quote inside doubled; CRLF or LF; a UTF-8 byte order mark dropped (option `encoding`: utf-8, windows-1252, iso-8859-1). The first row names the columns, matched as JSON's names are, unless `noHeader`, which fills the fields in the entity's order. An empty field is left out, so the record keeps its default. A list of values travels as its JSON text. Values are fitted as JSON's are. Writing gives a header row of the entity's fields that are one value (not the id, references, pictures, files or records inside) unless `noHeader`, then a row per record in Clarity's one form, quoted where needed, lines ended by CRLF. `read` cases give `fitted` or `error`, `write` cases `written`, word for word.",
